          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em homotopy cardinality
            or
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-groupoid cardinality
            of a (sufficiently “finite”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an invariant of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (a value assigned to its
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+class"} equivalence class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            = succeed "-groupoid)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Specifically, whereas cardinality counts elements in a set, the homotopy cardinality counts
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-equivalence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-morphism"} 3-equivalence
          %p
            This is closely related to the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            of a space or
            = succeed "-groupoid." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#groupoid_cardinality Groupoid cardinality
          %p
            The
            %strong cardinality
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  |X| = \sum_{[x] \in \pi_0(X)} \frac{1}{|Aut(x)|}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the sum is over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            classes of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi Aut
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |Aut(x)|
            is the cardinality of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            If this sum diverges, we say
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |X| = \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %strong tame
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+with+finite+homotopy+groups"} homotopy type with finite homotopy groups
          %h3#InfingroupoidCardinality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-Groupoid cardinality
          %p This is the special case of a more general definition:
          %p
            The groupoid cardinality of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            – equivalently the
            %strong Euler characteristic
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (that’s the same, due to the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+group"} simplicial
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  |X| := \sum_{[x] \in \pi_0(X)}\prod_{k = 1}^\infty |\pi_k(X,x)|^{(-1)^k}
                  \=
                  \\sum_{[x]}
                  \\frac{1}{|\pi_1(X,x)|}
                  |\pi_2(X,x)|
                  \\frac{1}{|\pi_3(X,x)|}
                  |\pi_4(X,x)|
                  \\cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            This corresponds to what is referred to as the
            %em homotopy Euler characteristic
            by
            %a{:href => "#Kontsevich88"} Kontsevich (1988)
            and the
            %em total homotopy order of a space
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Quinn95"} Quinn (1995)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete groupoid
                on a finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                elements. Then the groupoid cardinality of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is just the ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      |X| = n
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                of a finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                elements. Then
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      |\mathbf{B}G| = \frac{1}{k}
            %li
              %p
                More generally, for an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X//G
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\vert X\vert} {\vert G \vert}
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+formula"} class formula
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                be an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                elements. Then we can
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} deloop
                arbitrarily often and obtain the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Mac+Lane+objects"} Eilenberg-Mac Lane objects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[n]
                (or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[-n]
                depending on notational convention) that is concentrated in degree
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi k
                              %mtd
                                %mtext if
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi n
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mtext is even
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mi k
                              %mtd
                                %mtext if
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi n
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mtext is odd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      |\mathbf{B}^n A| =
                      \\begin{cases}
                      k           &amp; \text{if }\; n \;\text{ is even} \\
                      \\frac{1}{k} &amp; \text{if }\; n \;\text{ is odd}
                      \\end{cases}
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = core(FinSet)
                be the groupoid of finite sets and bijections – the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+number"} Euler number
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo !
                      %mo =
                      %mi e
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      |E| = \sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \frac{1}{|S_n|} = \sum_{n\in \mathbb{N}} \frac{1}{n!} = e
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E=(E_i)
                be a finite
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-groupoid"} omega-groupoid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in E_0
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                the cardinality of the set of
                = succeed "-cells" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                is independent of the vertex
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                can be calculated as
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo =
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                              %mi i
                            %mo #
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mi i
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |E|=\displaystyle{\prod_{i} \#(E_i)^{(-1)^i}}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                is a totally free crossed complex, this gives a very neat formula for the groupoid cardinality of the internal hom
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi HOM
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo ,
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} HOM(F,E)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-groupoids"} omega-groupoids
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-groupoid"} omega-groupoid
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+products"} Whitehead products
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                a suitable
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+group"} algebraic group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                a suitable
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} algebraic curve
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
                = succeed "-points" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔽
                          %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_q
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+G-principal+bundles"} moduli stack of G-principal bundles
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Bun
                        %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bun_G(X)
                is the subject of the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+conjectures+on+Tamagawa+numbers"} Weil conjectures on Tamagawa numbers
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+formula"} class formula
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Hoffnung"} Alexander Hoffnung
                %em Groupoidification Made Easy
                (web
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/groupoidification.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/12/groupoidification_made_easy.html"} blog
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher-dimensional algebra VII: Groupoidification
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.4305"} arxiv/0908.4305
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dolan"} James Dolan
                %em From Finite Sets to Feynman Diagrams
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0004133"}> arXiv
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jo%C3%A3o+Faria+Martins"}> João Faria Martins
                , On the homotopy type and the fundamental crossed complex of the skeletal filtration of a CW-complex (web
                %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v9/n1/a13/"} pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jo%C3%A3o+Faria+Martins"}> João Faria Martins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim Porter
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/18/4/18-04abs.html"} pdf
            %li#Kontsevich88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Rational conformal field theory and invariants of 3-dimensional manifolds
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ihes.fr/~maxim/TEXTS/3TQFT_and_RCFT.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Leinster"}> Tom Leinster
                ,
                %em The Euler characteristic of a category
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0610260"}> arXiv
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/week244.html"} TWF
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/02/this_weeks_finds_in_mathematic_5.html"} blog
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2006/10/euler_characteristic_of_a_cate.html"} blog
            %li
              %p
                Kazunori Noguchi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Euler characteristic of infinite acyclic categories with filtrations
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1004.2547"} arxiv/1004.2547
            %li#Quinn95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Quinn"}> Frank Quinn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Lectures on axiomatic topological quantum field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karen+Uhlenbeck"} Karen Uhlenbeck
                (eds.)
                %em Geometry and Quantum Field Theory
                %strong 1
                (1995) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/pcms/001"}> doi:10.1090/pcms/001
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Terence+Tao"}> Terence Tao
                , “
                %a{:href => "https://terrytao.wordpress.com/2017/04/13/counting-objects-up-to-isomorphism-groupoid-cardinality/"}> Counting objects up to isomorphism: groupoid cardinality
                ” (blog post), 13 April 2017.
            %li
              %p
                Lior Yanovski,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Homotopy Cardinality via Extrapolation of Morava-Euler Characteristics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.02603"} arXiv:2303.02603
